A||||0||Eric||The BEST way to bleed your clutch
Z||000000||Eric||05-27-99||04:58 PM||||Do you want to know the best way to bleed your clutch?  Weelll, I'll tell ya.  Buy a brake line vacuum pump.  It sucks all, yes thats right, all, the air out of the line.  You put the pump line on the slave bleeder screw and create a vacuum with the hand pump.  It draws fluid and air strait out of the bleeder screw, drops the fluid into a cup and expels the air out the top of the handle.  I bought the Mityvac Vacuum Pump from NAPA and paid about $30 for it.  The difference it made was incredible.  The pedal has good pressure from the beginning of the stroke to the floor.  Until now I can honestly say that I wasn't getting all of the air out by bleeding it in the traditional method.  By the way, beware of your bleeder screw.  If the system won't pressurize no matter how much you bleed it, that little screw could be leaking air.  I had a bad one on my new slave, so I had to give it the old one's screw as a transplant.  Just so you know, I never get  excited about a product like this, but I believe this is the solution to a huge problem for all of us Fiero owners (Well, maybe just us with the manual transmission). 
